  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0f3a2c8c7b8f4d9c9d5a3d11d5f50101, type: 3}
  m_Name: PokedexJerboa
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryId: jerboa
  commonName: Long-eared Jerboa
  scientificName: Euchoreutes naso
  icon: {fileID: 10904, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
  category: Mammal
  habitat: Arid Deserts & Sand Dunes
  height: 0.08 m
  weight: 0.03 kg
  diet: Insectivore
  rarity: Rare
  shortDescription: A tiny, nocturnal desert rodent instantly recognizable by its
    oversized ears, enormous hind legs, and exceptionally long, tufted tail.
  behaviorNotes: Highly active at night to avoid the desert heat. It moves in chaotic,
    erratic hops to confuse predators and uses its powerful legs to perform massive
    vertical leaps when startled.
  observationTips: Being so small, it is easiest to spot low to the ground near small
    desert shrubs or sand depressions. Listen closely for faint, rapid rustling or
    thumping in the sand.
  funFact: They have the largest ears relative to body size in the entire animal
    kingdom. Their ears are about two-thirds as long as their entire body!
  facts:
  - Their massive ears are highly vascularized, allowing them to radiate body heat
    away to stay cool without losing precious water.
  - Unlike many other rodents, their diet consists almost entirely of flying insects,
    which they catch by launching themselves into the air.
  - The long, tufted tail acts exactly like a counterweight and rudder, helping them
    balance and change directions instantly mid-hop.
